    "tips": "Measure in the thickest part of the meat, avoiding bone. Temperatures rise a few degrees while resting. Food safety note: For pork, chicken, and turkey, minimum safe target is 165°F (74°C) for poultry and 145°F (63°C) for whole-cut pork with a 3-minute rest."
